      "writtenOn": "2026-08-06T17:34:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When `prune\u003d\u003dPrune.False`, the skip-on-already-pending logic is entirely bypassed, and the stateMap growth problem is still present in that path. It\u0027s ok if you want to defer fixing that until a later change, but the commit message makes it sound like the problem is entirely solved and that\u0027s not accurate if it\u0027s only solved when `prune\u003d\u003dPrune.True`.",
