      "writtenOn": "2026-08-06T18:02:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I did think about it, but I wanted to keep the diff small. The Prune.FALSE path is the startup replay, which walks each waiting/ file exactly once, so no task is ever fired twice into the same pending push. So I don\u0027t think the stateMap growth is reachable there today. That said, Prune.FALSE can be used in another path in the future, so maybe I should just drop the Prune.TRUE condition at L255 and L272. WDYT? \n\nI\u0027ll also update the commit msg to not try to imply that the growth problem is fully solved, and instead describe the change as removing one source of it.",
      "parentUuid": "0c46b454_40cf21e3",
      "revId": "fabc4b75d2a245d9e9a699caaeb5690d8d633456",
